## Day-to-day

### Plan + apply infrastructure changes
```
./devops-ai.sh deploy-infra {{repo_name}}
```
The framework runs `terragrunt run --all plan`, summarizes the diff, and waits
for explicit approval before `apply`. For `env=prod`, approval requires
typing `apply prod`.

### Deploy a new application version
```
./devops-ai.sh deploy-app {{repo_name}}            # builds HEAD
./devops-ai.sh deploy-app {{repo_name}} v1.2.0     # builds a specific ref
```
Builds a `linux/amd64` image, pushes to ECR, updates the runtime, smoke-tests
the ALB target (or invokes the Lambda once), and writes a record to
`projects/{{repo_name}}/deploy/history.jsonl`.

### Stricter upgrade with prod gate
```
./devops-ai.sh upgrade {{repo_name}} v1.2.0
```
Same as `deploy-app`, but requires `apply prod` for prod and runs 5 successive
HTTP 2xx smoke checks on `/health`.

### Rollback to last known-good
```
./devops-ai.sh rollback {{repo_name}}
```
Looks up the most recent `result == success` entry in `history.jsonl`,
points the runtime at that image, and verifies health. Does not rebuild.

## Emergency

### Stop a stuck deploy
- ECS: `aws ecs update-service --force-new-deployment --desired-count 0`
- Lambda: `aws lambda update-function-code --image-uri <previous>`
- ASG: `aws autoscaling cancel-instance-refresh`

### Lost AWS state
- The Terragrunt state lives in S3 bucket `<state_bucket>` (see
  `projects/{{repo_name}}/iac/inputs.yaml`).
- S3 native lockfile (no DynamoDB needed). Stuck locks: `terragrunt force-unlock` or delete the lock object in S3.

